sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, R1-R4, decision swamp-vault-secrets (vault.get), orbit-gateway-renders-create-env (Gateway owns .env, no read-back), DECISIONS instance.sync_environment (vault after commit, @swamp/ssh from 209, no private-material fetch, no per-Node worker). docs/reference/environment-variables.md.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 14, 22 (cfgmgmt file for both files, its check as the end check; no script read, foreign-key check, report or assert step).
  %% Decided: Nick 2026-11-02, foreign-key protection at admission from the key names the Node agent reports; .env.testing only for an owned MySQL/PostgreSQL database, in the same file step.
  %% status: migrated
  %% Decided: Nick 2026-11-03, option 1: Orbit writes a managed .env as 0640 with group orbit-env, the agent's unit holds that group and reports key names only; a .env the agent can't read is not observed.
  %% command: env:sync
  %% kind: instance.sync_environment
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Instance Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: env:sync --instance=42<br/>--json
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit env:sync --instance=42`
  %%> - syntax: `env:sync --instance=SELECTOR [--force] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Instance: a numeric Instance ID or the exact domain of its Route
  %%> - `--force` overwrites keys that only the Node's `.env` holds
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, render .env<br/>Instance 42 · task #5131
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12, the Node of Instance 42
  %%> - Instance 42 is active, on a Node with exactly one active `app-dev` or `app-prod` role
  %%> - Instance 42 has stored configuration (`env.configuration_missing` otherwise)
  %%> - a stored `{{instance.domain}}` needs a settled Route (`env.reference_unavailable` otherwise)
  %%> - no other task holds Instance 42; the Gateway holds one lock per Instance and waits briefly for a busy one
  %%> Checks foreign keys:
  %%> - compares the `.env` key names the Node agent reported with the stored and owned keys; no values are read
  %%> - Orbit writes a managed `.env` as 0640 with group `orbit-env`, which the agent's unit holds
  %%> - a `.env` the agent can't read, such as a hand-made 0600 file or a link, or a silent agent, leaves the names not observed
  %%> - when the agent reports that Git tracks `.env.testing`, the plan writes none
  %%> Renders .env:
  %%> - every stored key in sorted order, as a quoted value
  %%> - `{{instance.domain}}` from the Route, `{{instance.environment}}` from the Node role
  %%> Renders .env.testing:
  %%> - only when Instance 42 owns a database on a MySQL or PostgreSQL server
  %%> - the same `.env` with `APP_ENV=testing` and the test database credentials
  %%> - SQLite: none; `phpunit.xml` (`:memory:`) decides
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5131 recorded with the full intent and the sha256 of each rendered file
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  opt keys not observed, or .env holds foreign keys
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>keys not observed or foreign
    %%> When:
    %%> - `env.keys_not_observed`: the Node agent has not reported the `.env` key names, and `--force` is not set
    %%> - `env.sync_would_drop_keys`: the Node's `.env` holds keys that Orbit neither stores nor wrote, and `--force` is not set
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the refusal names the keys; no task and no run start
    %%> Next:
    %%> - foreign keys: `env:import` adopts them first, or `env:sync --force` replaces the file
    %%> - not observed, as for a `.env` written 0600 before this mode: `env:import`, then `env:sync --force`, which drops nothing and writes the file 0640
  end
  GW->>SW: Push .env to the vault<br/>vault: env-5131, env-testing-5131
  %%> Why:
  %%> - `.env` holds secrets, which travel only through the vault (R3)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - after the task commits, pushes the rendered files into Swamp's vault on Node 209
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the run reads them with `vault.get`; no step calls the Gateway back
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-environment
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - the account, the application directory, the file paths and the expected sha256 of each file
  %%> - the key names Orbit wrote last time, which it may remove
  %%> - production only: the release path and the Processes with `restart_on_deploy`
  %%> - secrets only as vault key names
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5131
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Create the orbit-env group<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/group
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates the system group when the Node lacks it; the Node agent's unit holds it
  SW->>N: Write .env, .env.testing<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file · 0640
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209 with `@swamp/ssh` and the official `@swamp/cfgmgmt/file` behavior; nothing is copied to the Node
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the rendered `.env` from `vault.get env-5131`, mode `0640`
  %%> - with an owned MySQL or PostgreSQL database, writes `.env.testing` in the same step, replacing its content; no merge
  %%> - a Git-tracked `.env.testing` stays untouched: admission planned none
  %%> - leaves a file that already matches in place
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - the Instance account, in its own directory, so no root write follows a link the account placed
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - renders nothing; the Gateway already rendered the files
  SW->>N: Set the group orbit-env<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · chgrp -h
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - root runs `chgrp -h orbit-env` on the written files; `-h` never follows a link
  %%> - the Node agent's unit holds `orbit-env`, so it may read the `.env` key names; it never reads `.env.testing`
  Note over SW: Check the written file<br/>assert · file state
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - compares the sha256 the file behavior recorded for each file with the rendered one
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the sync only counts when the Node holds exactly what the Gateway rendered
  %%> - a rerun writes and checks again
  opt production Instance
    SW->>N: Refresh the runtime<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · in order
    %%> When:
    %%> - on every production sync, also when `.env` did not change
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs `php artisan config:cache` as the Instance account in the release, as one `@swamp/ssh exec`, when the release has a config cache; an uncached release stays uncached
    %%> - reloads the PHP-FPM pool to reset OPcache
    %%> - restarts the running Processes that have `restart_on_deploy`
    %%> - each action is one `@swamp/ssh exec` command, one at a time
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - development Instances: they only get the file
  end
  alt every file matches
    N-->>SW: files match, refreshed
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - whether each file changed, and the runtime refresh status
    %%> Not returned:
    %%> - no values and no file content
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · changed flags
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the run's outputs; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>owned keys · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the synced key names become the keys Orbit owns on Instance 42
    %%> - task #5131 succeeds with `changed`, the testing status and the refresh status
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0<br/>file write or check fails
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, a write fails, or a file does not match after the write
    %%> How:
    %%> - the failing step ends the run with its own exit code; there is no report step
    %%> - production: the config cache or the Process restart fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep stored values<br/>task failed · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - stored values and the owned-key list stay as they were
    %%> - task #5131 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a refused file stays unchanged; a failed cache build keeps the old cache
    %%> - a file already written stays; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix the cause, then run `env:sync` again; it is a new task
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5131
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
